<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσοσκελ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with equal legs</i>, esp.
			in Geom., <i>having two sides equal, isosceles</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίγωνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					54a
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APo.</u>
				41b14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of numbers,
				<i>that can be divided into two equal parts, even</i> (as
				<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i> + <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>), opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκαληνός</span>, odd (as
				<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>
			=
			<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i> + <i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				12d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Rhet., of
			periods, <i>containing equal members</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Inv.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> Medic.,
				<i>having equal tails</i>, of a bandage, <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				48.62
			</span></i> tit.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
